---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Planetary Science Cheat Sheet | Free Solar System, Exoplanets, Formation"
  description="Complete planetary science cheat sheet with solar system, exoplanets, and formation. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Planetary Science<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Solar system, exoplanets, and formation. From protoplanetary disks to habitable zones.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Solar System</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Planets</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Planet</th><th>Type</th><th>Key Feature</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Mercury</td><td>Terrestrial</td><td>Smallest, no atmosphere</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Venus</td><td>Terrestrial</td><td>Thick CO₂ atmosphere, run温室</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Earth</td><td>Terrestrial</td><td>Life, liquid water</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Mars</td><td>Terrestrial</td><td>Thin atmosphere, polar caps</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jupiter</td><td>Gas giant</td><td>Great Red Spot, 95 moons</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Saturn</td><td>Gas giant</td><td>Rings, low density</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Uranus</td><td>Ice giant</td><td>Tilted axis, faint rings</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Neptune</td><td>Ice giant</td><td>Strongest winds</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Orbital Mechanics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Kepler's Laws</h3>
        <pre><code>1. Elliptical orbits (focus at Sun)
2. Equal areas in equal times (A = const)
3. T² ∝ a³ (a = semi-major axis)
T² = (4π²/GM)a³</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Orbital Velocity</h3>
        <pre><code>v = √(GM/r) (circular)
Escape: v_e = √(2GM/r)
Roche limit: d = 2.46 R_p(ρ_p/ρ_m)^(1/3)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Exoplanets</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Detection Methods</h3>
        <pre><code>Transit: brightness dip (Kepler, TESS)
Radial velocity: star wobble (Doppler)
Direct imaging: direct observation
Microlensing: gravitational lensing
Astrometry: star position change</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Habitable Zone</h3>
        <pre><code>Luminosity-dependent zone
Water can exist as liquid
Not too hot, not too cold
Conservative: 0.95-1.67 AU for Sun
Optimistic: 0.75-1.77 AU for Sun</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Planetary Formation</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Core Accretion Model</h3>
        <pre><code>Protoplanetary disk: gas + dust
Dust → planetesimals → protoplanets
Terrestrial planets: inner disk (rock/metal)
Gas giants: outer disk (gas/ice capture)
Snow line: where water freezes</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
